From: Lithify <lithify@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] connect: take a playlist's context from the playlist service

Context resolve leaves out the podcast episodes of a playlist that mixes them with tracks. The
official clients list those episodes all the same, and a play command picks one by its uid
alone (skip_to with an empty track_uri). librespot then found no such track and started the
playlist's first one instead ("Failed to resolve index by Some(Uid(..)), using fallback index:
None"). The playlist service lists every item, each with the uid the clients know it by, so a
playlist's context comes from it; context resolve is asked as before when the service gives no
whole answer.

---
